SRC/eff_qp -- changes made for the OSK freeware collection  qp.c     qp hands the expanded command to $SHELL.  It passed the options           "-ny -nl" first -- options of the zsh it was written for, which           no shell here has -- and ksh answered by doing nothing, bash           with `-y: bad option'.  It now passes the command line as the           shell's one argument and nothing else, which is how both ksh           and Microware's shell take a command.  With no SHELL set it           names `shell' where it named `zsh'.  Rebuilt -qm, 2026-09-26.           The original is qp.c.ori.